First Lady of the United States.

00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:11.285
Let's welcome Dr. Jill Biden, everybody!

00:00:11.285 --> 00:00:12.400
(audience clapping)

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.624
(piano music)

00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:15.498
- Hi everybody!

00:00:15.498 --> 00:00:17.250
- [Kelly] Hello, hello!

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.230
High five from afar!

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.670
- [Jill] Hi, how are you?
- [Kelly] You look beautiful!

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:21.660
- [Jill] Well so do you!
- I know, it's like we dressed

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.357
like we look like a beautiful
garden I feel like, yes.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.160
And well have a seat.
- [Jill] Thanks!

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.780
- I'm pretty sure this
is the furthest interview

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:30.190
I've ever given so if I shout I'm sorry.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.910
- [Jill] That's okay.
- We're keepin' it safe.

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:32.743
We're keepin' it safe.

00:00:32.743 --> 00:00:33.620
How're you doin' today?

00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.340
- I'm doin' great, how 'bout you?

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.500
- I'm so lucky and fortunate to be here.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.430
I cannot say thank you enough.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.040
- Yes, welcome to my
house, the people's house,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.170
your house.
- [Kelly] I know,

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.488
it's crazy you live here, but you're,

00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:46.838
you're also the spotlight singer today.

00:00:46.838 --> 00:00:48.800
I actually did not know this song.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.760
I was very-
- [Jill] Oh no kidding!

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.360
- I always get excited
when people pick songs

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.670
I didn't know before and
then I get to learn them.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.610
So the original version, the
Young Bloods, I think, right?

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.840
- [Jill] That's exactly right.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.040
So you love this song?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.730
- I love this song because you know

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:03.510
I think it's so perfect for today,

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.630
you know, because I think our
country has been so divided

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:10.040
and you know, now if we
could just come together

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.433
as a country and solve our differences.

00:01:13.863 --> 00:01:15.520
And I first heard it, course this is why

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.960
you haven't heard it, I
heard it in the sixties.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.670
So, you know, there was the Vietnam war

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:22.350
the civil rights movement.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.740
People, it was a similar time
where people were divided and

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.490
and the Young Bloods came out

00:01:27.490 --> 00:01:30.570
with this song and everybody
would be singing it, you know

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:32.607
everybody come together.

00:01:32.607 --> 00:01:33.660
So, strong message.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.800
- Yeah, it's a beautiful thing.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:35.860
And I feel like it's one

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.160
of those things where I'm like,
Oh, this was a cool moment.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.890
Then it's then I also get kind of sad.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:42.472
Cause I'm like, wow, this
message is relevant again.

00:01:42.472 --> 00:01:44.190
Like I kind of get really sad

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.920
about that sometimes
too, but it's, it's nice.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.860
I think that's why I love
being a part of music so much

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.790
because we're able to
create something that even

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.190
if you're from different walks
of life, you can, you know

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:55.040
come together and love a song together

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.140
and sing a song together.

00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.180
- Well I could listen
to your voice all day.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.230
- [Kelly] Oh, well, thank you.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.720
I've had about four and
a half hours of sleep.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:04.273
So you got my raspy Janis Joplin version.

00:02:04.273 --> 00:02:05.670
- See, Janis Joplin.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:06.880
She was from my era as well.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.300
- [Kelly] I love Janis Joplin.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.180
I'm Texan, I think you come
out of the womb loving her.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.210
Well, you've said, I, I read your book.

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:14.630
I love "Where the Light Enters"

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:16.130
what a great quote that came from too.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:16.963
- [Jill] Thank you.

00:02:16.963 --> 00:02:18.420
- Yeah. It was really, really great.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.220
And it- and it's something honestly,

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:23.190
separate from this question
to aspire to family-wise, um.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:24.770
I found that inspiring.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:26.550
So thank you for that.

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.460
And, and also you said that you-

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:31.500
you're like an introvert
married to an extrovert,

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.730
um, but you're pretty strong and fearless

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.040
because I did see something

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.730
